   {"on": "you alone, as it seems to us, judging from these resolutions, regard what is future as more certain than what is before your eyes", "text": "The Athenians' last word is about sight. Trust what you can see. It is, in a way, Thucydides' own method: the clearest data, not romance. That is what makes the dialogue so uncomfortable."},
   {"on": "the Melians surrendered at discretion to the Athenians, who put to death all the grown men whom they took, and sold the women and children for slaves", "text": "Thucydides tells it in one flat sentence, without comment. That is his comment. He has given the Athenians every argument; now he shows what the arguments were for."}
